+This will end the request with `400 - Bad Request` status code and the following JSON response, sent with `Content-Type: application/problem+json` ([RFC 9457](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457) problem details):
 
 ```json
 {
   "date": "2025-06-05T04:20:00.0Z",
-  "status": 400,
   "statusText": "Bad Request",
   "message": "Invalid user input",
   "data": {
     "field": "email"
-  }
+  },
+  "type": "about:blank",
+  "title": "Bad Request",
+  "status": 400,
+  "detail": "Invalid user input"
 }
 ```
 
+The RFC 9457 members (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail` and `instance`) always reflect the error, so `body` cannot override them. The fields that existed before (`message`, `data`, `body` and `statusText`) are kept as extension members. `message` is the legacy name of `detail`, and new clients should read `detail`.
+
 ### `HTTPError` Fields
 
 - `status`: HTTP status code in the range 200–599.
